.Dd February 26, 2026
.Dt UNIQ 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm uniq
.Nd report or omit repeated lines
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cduDiz
.Op Fl f Ar fields
.Op Fl s Ar chars
.Op Fl w Ar chars
.Op Ar input Op Ar output
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility reads the specified
.Ar input
file comparing adjacent lines, and writes a copy of each unique
input line to the
.Ar output
file.
If
.Ar input
is a single dash
.Pq Sq -
or absent, the standard input is read.
If
.Ar output
is absent, standard output is used for output.
.Pp
The second and succeeding copies of identical adjacent input
lines are not written.
Repeated lines in the input will not be detected if they are
not adjacent, so it may be necessary to sort the files first.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c , Fl Fl count
Precede each output line with the count of the number of
times the line occurred in the input, followed by a single
space.
.It Fl d , Fl Fl repeated
Only output lines that are repeated in the input.
.It Fl D
Output all lines that are repeated in the input.
Unlike
.Fl d ,
which outputs one copy per group,
.Fl D
outputs every repeated line.
.It Fl f Ar fields , Fl Fl skip-fields Ns = Ns Ar fields
Ignore the first
.Ar fields
fields in each input line when doing comparisons.
A field is a string of non-blank characters separated from
adjacent fields by blanks.
Field numbers are one based, i.e., the first field is field one.
.It Fl i , Fl Fl ignore-case
Case insensitive comparison of lines.
.It Fl s Ar chars , Fl Fl skip-chars Ns = Ns Ar chars
Ignore the first
.Ar chars
characters in each input line when doing comparisons.
If specified in conjunction with the
.Fl f
option, the first
.Ar chars
characters after the first
.Ar fields
fields will be ignored.
.It Fl u , Fl Fl unique
Only output lines that are not repeated in the input.
.It Fl w Ar chars , Fl Fl check-chars Ns = Ns Ar chars
Compare no more than
.Ar chars
characters in each input line
.Pq or after any skipping due to Fl f No or Fl s .
.It Fl z , Fl Fl zero-terminated
Delimit lines with NUL characters rather than newlines.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Display help information and exit.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Output version information and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std uniq
.Sh EXAMPLES
Remove adjacent duplicate lines from a file:
.Pp
.Dl $ sort names.txt | uniq
.Pp
Show duplicate lines with their counts:
.Pp
.Dl $ sort words.txt | uniq -c | sort -rn | head
.Pp
Show only lines that appear more than once:
.Pp
.Dl $ sort data.txt | uniq -d
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr comm 1 ,
.Xr sort 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An "vibeutils implementation by Travis Cole"
